ais + Saut-d'Eau","group of communes (reported together)","Centre department",[[2,0,0,0,[0],[[0,[8]],[4,[2]],[2,[4]],[3,[2]]]]]],["Cité Soleil + Croix-des-Bouquets","group of communes (reported together)","West department",[[14,0,1,0,[1],[[0,[116]],[4,[4]],[1,[5]],[2,[95]],[3,[12]]]],[14,0,2,0,[2],[[0,[478]],[5,[307]],[7,[294]],[8,[13]],[9,[171]],[13,[36]],[10,[8]],[11,[72]],[12,[55]]]]]],["Arcahaie + Cabaret","group of communes (reported together)","West department",[[2,0,2,0,[2],[[0,[6]]]]]]]},"rows":108,"sources":{"binuh_qr_2025q4":{"name":"Quarterly Report on the Human Rights Situation in Haiti, October-December 2025","publisher":"United Nations Integrated Office in Haiti (BINUH), Human Rights Service (HRS), jointly with OHCHR","url":"https://binuh.unmissions.org/en/rapports-sur-la-situation-des-droits-de-lhomme","licence":"no licence stated (only photo credits are marked ©)","years":"2025 Q4","notes":"Figures read from the narrative and footnotes of section 1.1 (gang violence) of the report; each figure is quoted in raw/quotes.txt. These are people killed by gangs as documented by the UN, stated as minimums (\"at least\"); they are NOT police-recorded homicides and they exclude the much larger numbers killed during security-force operations and by self-defence groups, which the report gives only nationally. Areas are those the report itself uses; where it reports two communes together (e.g. Carrefour + Gressier) the row is kept as one area with no shape. Breakdowns (men/women/boys/girls, associated / not associated with gangs) are exactly as in the footnotes; nothing was added up by us. Zero rows are only where the report states that no gang victims/abuses were documented in that commune."},"binuh_qr_2026q1":{"name":"Quarterly Report on the Human Rights Situation in Haiti, January-March 2026","publisher":"United Nations Integrated Office in Haiti (BINUH), Human Rights Service (HRS), jointly with OHCHR","url":"https://binuh.unmissions.org/en/rapports-sur-la-situation-des-droits-de-lhomme","licence":"no licence stated (only photo credits are marked ©)","years":"2026 Q1","notes":"Figures read from the narrative and footnotes of section 1.1 (gang violence) of the report; each figure is quoted in raw/quotes.txt. These are people killed by gangs as documented by the UN, stated as minimums (\"at least\"); they are NOT police-recorded homicides and they exclude the much larger numbers killed during security-force operations and by self-defence groups, which the report gives only nationally. Areas are those the report itself uses; where it reports two communes together (e.g. Carrefour + Gressier) the row is kept as one area with no shape. Breakdowns (men/women/boys/girls, associated / not associated with gangs) are exactly as in the footnotes; nothing was added up by us. Zero rows are only where the report states that no gang victims/abuses were documented in that commune."},"binuh_qr_2026q2":{"name":"Quarterly Report on the Human Rights Situation in Haiti, April-June 2026","publisher":"United Nations Integrated Office in Haiti (BINUH), Human Rights Service (HRS), jointly with OHCHR","url":"https://binuh.unmissions.org/en/rapports-sur-la-situation-des-droits-de-lhomme","licence":"no licence stated (only photo credits are marked ©)","years":"2026 Q2","notes":"Figures read from the narrative and footnotes of section 1.1 (gang violence) of the report; each figure is quoted in raw/quotes.txt. These are people killed by gangs as documented by the UN, stated as minimums (\"at least\"); they are NOT police-recorded homicides and they exclude the much larger numbers killed during security-force operations and by self-defence groups, which the report gives only nationally. Areas are those the report itself uses; where it reports two communes together (e.g. Carrefour + Gressier) the row is kept as one area with no shape. Breakdowns (men/women/boys/girls, associated / not associated with gangs) are exactly as in the footnotes; nothing was added up by us. Zero rows are only where the report states that no gang victims/abuses were documented in that commune. Q2 2026 Artibonite: the text gives 73 killed but footnote 15 lists 68 not associated with gangs plus 2 men associated with gangs (=70); both kept as printed."}},"dict":{"b":["Total","Girls","Men","Women","Boys","Associated with gangs","Associated with gangs: boys","Associated with gangs: men","Associated with gangs: women","Not associated with gangs","Not associated with gangs: girls","Not associated with gangs: men","Not associated with gangs: women","Not associated with gangs: boys"],"m":["People killed by gangs (gang violence), at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service (targeted killings for breaking gang rules, opposing gangs or as punishment)","Members of the population killed by stray bullets fired during gang celebrations (Nov-Dec), at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed by gangs (gang violence), at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","Deaths in incidents involving gangs, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","Victims linked to gang attacks documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service (source: no victims documented)","Residents killed in gang attacks, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","Victims of gang-related abuses documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service (source: no gang-related abuses documented)","People killed in gang-related violence (footnote 10), as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed in gang-related incidents (footnote 9), as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed in gang-related violence (footnote 11), as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","Members of the population killed in gang attacks, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed as a result of gang attacks, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed as a result of gang violence, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","Deaths from gang violence, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service","People killed by gang violence, at least, as documented by the BINUH Human Rights Service"],"u":["count"],"s":["binuh_qr_2025q4","binuh_qr_2026q1","binuh_qr_2026q2"],"c":["2025 Q4 (Oct-Dec)","2026 Q1 (Jan-Mar)","2026 Q2 (Apr-Jun)"]},"problems":"The UN BINUH \"Haiti Security and Crime Statistics\" dataset on HDX (binuh-scstats, CC BY-IGO) gives intentional homicides by month for the whole country only (no department field), so it was not used. The Police Nationale d'Haïti publishes no open statistics. BINUH/OHCHR quarterly human-rights reports give people killed in gang violence by department in PDF narrative/figures; these were not extracted (gang-violence killings, figures mostly in graphics). Retry (17 Oct): re-checked HDX (only binuh-scstats, national monthly, last updated 2026-03-17; copy kept in raw/ for reference) and a World Bank public-sector dataset; BINUH quarterly human-rights press releases (e.g. Q2 2026, 25 Aug 2026) give national totals and qualitative mentions of departments, no department counts in text; department breakdowns appear only as chart images in the OHCHR/BINUH quarterly PDFs and are gang-violence casualties rather than police-recorded homicide. No PNH, IHSI or Ministry of Health subnational homicide table found. THIRD PASS 17 Oct: used the BINUH quarterly human-rights reports (UN route) for the three most recent quarters, extracting the commune/department counts of people killed by gangs from the text and footnotes. Not extracted: Q2 2025 and Q3 2025 reports (downloaded and read; same kind of narrative, areas reported inconsistently, left for a later pass), the 2025 annual report (A/HRC/61/74, department shares only), and the department percentage charts (they mix killed and injured from all perpetrators including police operations). No PNH or health-ministry figures by department found.","unmatched":5,"shapes":{"shapes_ADM1.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen HTI ADM1","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/HTI/ADM1/geoBoundaries-HTI-ADM1_simplified.geojson","licence":"CC BY 4.0"},"shapes_ADM3.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen HTI ADM3","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/HTI/ADM3/geoBoundaries-HTI-ADM3_simplified.geojson","licence":"CC BY 4.0"}}}